{"company":{"ticker":"PLTR","name":"Palantir Technologies","sector":"Technology","industry":"Software","size":"large","cik":1321655},"scores":{"growth":96.0,"quality":84.0,"value":25.0,"acceleration":97.0,"price_momentum":79.0,"reality":93.0,"pricing":78.0},"strategist":{"ticker":"PLTR","opportunity_score":69.0,"components":{"structural_trend":63.0,"capital_flow":83.0,"acceleration":97.0,"quality":84.0,"valuation":25.0,"estimate_revisions":null,"management_commentary":null,"narrative_acceleration":null,"insider_institutional":null},"weights":{"structural_trend":0.2,"capital_flow":0.1,"acceleration":0.15,"quality":0.15,"valuation":0.15,"estimate_revisions":0.1,"management_commentary":0.05,"narrative_acceleration":0.05,"insider_institutional":0.05},"coverage":0.75,"unavailable":{"estimate_revisions":"Estimate-revision feed (Phase 2)","management_commentary":"Earnings Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","narrative_acceleration":"Narrative Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","insider_institutional":"Form 4 / 13F ingestion (Phase 2)"},"reality":84.0,"narrative":66.0,"pricing":69.0,"expectations_gap":15.0,"macro_fit":53.0,"sector_rotation":73.0,"theme_pricing":49.0,"checks":[{"label":"Revenue accelerating","ok":true,"evidence":"TTM growth +78.9% vs +67.7% prior quarter"},{"label":"FCF improving","ok":true,"evidence":"FCF growth +96.5%, FCF margin +54.6%"},{"label":"ROIC expanding","ok":true,"evidence":"ROIC +214.3%, incremental ROIC +500.0%"},{"label":"Margins expanding","ok":true,"evidence":"Operating margin +42.8% (+2624 bps YoY)"},{"label":"Theme exposure strengthening","ok":true,"evidence":"Exposure-weighted theme trend 63.0"},{"label":"Capital rotating toward sector","ok":true,"evidence":"Technology rotation score +73"},{"label":"Valuation below own history","ok":true,"evidence":"Cheapness vs 5y history 84.0/100"},{"label":"Valuation below sector peers","ok":false,"evidence":"Sector-relative value score 25.0"},{"label":"Balance sheet strong","ok":true,"evidence":"Net debt/EBITDA -3.5"},{"label":"Not diluting shareholders","ok":false,"evidence":"Diluted share count +1.8% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"Palantir Technologies (PLTR) screens at opportunity 69.0 with an expectations gap of 15.0. Reality 84.0 reflects +78.9% TTM revenue growth, +42.8% operating margin and +214.3% ROIC; pricing 69.0 reflects a rich multiple and strong price momentum. Primary theme exposure: AI Software & Agents (trend 71.0). Macro fit for Technology in a Goldilocks regime is 53.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced for sustained high growth and margin expansion; little room for disappointment.","evidence":["EV/Sales 73.3x (32.0th pct of own 5y range)","P/E 153x","FCF yield 0.7%","PEG 0.5","12m return +7%, -7% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["Reality (84.0) is running ahead of what is priced (69.0): an expectations gap of +15 pts."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-08-04)","AI Software & Agents: evidence that 'Trust, integration into workflows, proprietary data' is easing via Platforms owning the system of record and the data","Continued rotation into Technology"],"risks":["Valuation leaves little room for execution slips."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 55% (currently 78.9%)","ROIC falls below 161% (currently 214.3%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200 bps YoY (currently 42.8%)","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +73)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","AI Software & Agents theme trend drops below 45"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":0.5524,"current":0.7892},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":1.6074,"current":2.1432},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":0.2624472267311754},{"id":"rotation","label":"Technology rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-20,"consecutive":2,"current":73.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":48.599999999999994},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":26.2},{"id":"theme","label":"AI Software & Agents theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"ai-software-agents","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":71.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"ai-software-agents","theme":"AI Software & Agents","weight":0.9,"order":1,"effective":0.9},{"theme_id":"defense-modernization","theme":"Defense Modernization","weight":0.3,"order":1,"effective":0.3}],"llm":{"thesis":"Palantir is compounding at a rate that few large-caps have ever sustained \u2014 TTM revenue +78.9% and accelerating from +67.7%, operating margin 42.8% (+2,624bps YoY), FCF margin 54.6% on essentially zero capex ($42m against $6.16bn revenue) and $9.4bn net cash with zero debt. The under-appreciated fact is that the 12-month return is only +6.9% while revenue nearly doubled: the multiple has compressed hard (EV/Sales 73x sits at the 32nd percentile of its own 5-year range versus a 92.7x median; P/FCF 137x versus a 286.5x median), so the last year has been a de-rating absorbed by fundamentals, not a melt-up. The engine's reality score (84) running 15 points ahead of pricing (69) is consistent with that: the business is outrunning the multiple even at absurd absolute levels. The offset is unambiguous \u2014 EV/Sales 73x, EV/EBITDA 169x and a 0.7% FCF yield price zero tolerance for a growth step-down, and the sector-relative value score of 25 says PLTR is still the most expensive asset in an expensive sector. This is a momentum-plus-quality position sized for volatility, not a valuation-support position.","fundamental_read":"Growth is accelerating (78.9% vs 67.7% prior) at the same time margins expand (op margin +2,624bps YoY) and cash conversion exceeds 1.1x \u2014 that combination is rare and implies operating leverage on an already-built platform rather than growth bought with spend. ROIC of 214% with incremental ROIC pinned at 500% reflects a near-capex-free model ($42m capex, 0.7% of revenue) funded by a $9.4bn net cash balance sheet. The blemishes are non-cash and dilutive rather than operational: SBC is 13.6% of revenue and diluted shares grew 1.8% YoY, and net margin (49%) exceeding operating margin (42.8%) on a 5% tax rate means reported EPS is flattered by interest income and NOL/tax benefits \u2014 so the 153x P/E overstates the durability of bottom-line quality relative to the 137x P/FCF.","technical_read":"Clean uptrend: price 191.79 above the 20/50/200 SMAs (177/162/152), 50>200, MACD histogram positive, and +26.2% extended above the 200-day. RSI 66.9 is strong but not yet a blow-off, and the stock is only -7.4% from the 52-week high after a +69% three-month move \u2014 a breakout to new highs is the natural next technical event, but the 26% extension above trend means a mean-reversion toward the 50-day (~162, roughly -16%) would be routine, not thesis-breaking.","market_expectation":"At 73x EV/Sales and a 0.7% FCF yield, the market is underwriting many years of 40%+ compounding with margins holding above 40% \u2014 essentially that Palantir becomes the system of record for enterprise and government AI workflows and that competition never compresses pricing. Yet the 12-month return of +6.9% against +78.9% revenue growth shows the market has simultaneously been de-rating the multiple, which implies the consensus is already discounting a future deceleration and is unwilling to pay the prior peak sales multiple. The setup is therefore 'priced for perfection in absolute terms, priced for deceleration in relative-to-own-history terms.'","what_market_misses":["Multiple compression has been doing the work: EV/Sales at the 32nd percentile of its own 5y range and P/FCF at the 0th percentile mean the stock has de-rated ~40%+ versus its own history while growth accelerated \u2014 every quarter of 70%+ growth mechanically cheapens it if the price is flat.","Revenue acceleration at $6bn+ scale (+11.2pts sequentially) is the hardest metric to fake and almost never mean-reverts in a single quarter; models built on a smooth deceleration curve are likely too low for the next two prints.","The capital intensity is close to zero \u2014 capex is 0.7% of revenue with 1.11x FCF conversion \u2014 so unlike AI hardware and hyperscaler peers, incremental growth requires no balance-sheet funding; a $9.4bn net cash position with no debt makes the business self-financing through any funding-market stress.","Defense Modernization exposure is carried at only 0.3 weight versus 0.9 for AI Software; government/defense budget durability is a second, less-correlated demand stream that likely underwrites the growth floor better than the pure AI-software narrative implies.","Reported net margin (49%) exceeding operating margin (42.8%) on a 5% tax rate is a hidden negative the P/E hides \u2014 normalized taxes would materially raise the true earnings multiple, so bulls citing 153x P/E are citing a flattered number.","Sector-relative value 25 versus own-history cheapness 84 is a real tell: PLTR is cheap only against itself. If the Technology rotation score (+73) reverses, the relative-value anchor offers no support."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (~90 days after the 2026-08-04 filing): a fourth consecutive acceleration print, or the first deceleration, resolves the entire debate.","A breakout above the 52-week high (-7.4% away) with volume against the 27.8m 20-day average would confirm the +69% 3-month trend and likely trigger momentum/index flows.","Continued Technology sector rotation (+73, the only sector above +10 apart from Energy at +8) concentrating capital into a narrow set of AI winners.","Evidence that the AI Software & Agents bottleneck \u2014 trust, workflow integration, proprietary data \u2014 is easing in favor of platforms that own the system of record, which would validate the 0.9-weight theme exposure.","Defense Modernization contract awards, which are lumpy, high-visibility and currently under-weighted in the theme mix."],"risks":["EV/Sales 73x and a 0.7% FCF yield leave no cushion: a single quarter of growth below expectations can compress the multiple 30-40% without any change to the business.","SBC at 13.6% of revenue and +1.8% annual dilution mean GAAP-clean FCF is meaningfully overstated as owner earnings; persistent dilution is a slow tax on holders.","The regime read is effectively a coin flip \u2014 Goldilocks 26.3% versus Stagflation 23.7% and Contraction 24.9% \u2014 so the 'Goldilocks' label carries low conviction and macro fit is only 53/100; a rate/liquidity shock hits the longest-duration equity hardest.","Price is 26.2% above the 200-day; crowded momentum positioning makes drawdowns violent even absent fundamental news.","Government revenue concentration cuts both ways: budget continuing resolutions or procurement slowdowns can create lumpy, unmodelled quarters.","Estimate-revision and management-guidance feeds are not connected, so two of the twelve checks are blind \u2014 the thesis rests on trailing rather than forward evidence."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 55% (currently 78.9%) \u2014 acceleration is the core of the thesis.","Operating margin compresses more than 200bps YoY from 42.8%, signalling growth is being bought rather than earned.","FCF margin falls below ~40% or FCF conversion drops below 0.9x, indicating cash quality deterioration behind GAAP earnings.","Dilution accelerates above ~3% annually or SBC exceeds ~18% of revenue.","Price closes >10% below the 200-day (~137) with negative relative strength.","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +73).","AI Software & Agents theme trend drops below 45 (currently 71).","Combined Stagflation + Contraction regime probability exceeds 55% (currently 48.6%)."],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Hyperscalers and GPU/neocloud providers: Palantir spends only $42m of capex on $6.16bn of revenue, meaning its compute and inference footprint is rented \u2014 its growth converts directly into third-party cloud and accelerated-compute revenue.","Data-center power, grid and cooling suppliers: the inference load behind AI agent workflows is an energy problem, and Energy is the only other sector with a positive rotation score (+8), suggesting this linkage is under-owned.","Systems integrators and consulting firms: the forward-deployed-engineer model is human-capital constrained; partners who can scale deployment headcount capture the implementation spend Palantir cannot staff itself.","Government-cloud and accreditation infrastructure (FedRAMP/IL-level hosting, identity and zero-trust security vendors): every classified or regulated deployment drags compliance infrastructure spend behind it.","Data pipeline, ETL and observability vendors: the binding constraint cited in the theme evidence is proprietary data integration, which is a wedge for whoever cleans and moves the data before the ontology layer sees it.","Defense primes and sub-tier suppliers whose programs the software layer is embedded in \u2014 software modernization budgets are usually appropriated alongside platform budgets."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"TTM revenue grew 78.9%, accelerating from 67.7% in the prior quarter.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Operating margin is 42.8%, up 2,624bps YoY; FCF margin 54.6% on $42m of capex; net cash $9.4bn with zero debt.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"EV/Sales is 73.3x (32nd percentile of own 5y range vs 92.7x median) and P/FCF is 137x (0th percentile vs 286.5x median).","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"12-month return is +6.9% while 3-month return is +69%; price is -7.4% from the 52-week high and 26.2% above the 200-day.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"SBC is 13.6% of revenue and diluted shares rose 1.8% YoY; tax rate is 5%.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"The market is underwriting many years of 40%+ growth with 40%+ margins at a 0.7% FCF yield.","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"Flat 12-month price against ~79% revenue growth means the market has already been discounting a future growth deceleration.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Net margin exceeding operating margin on a 5% tax rate means reported EPS is flattered by interest income and tax benefits, so the true normalized earnings multiple is higher than 153x.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Near-zero capex with 1.11x FCF conversion means growth is self-funding and independent of external capital markets.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Revenue acceleration at $6bn+ scale rarely reverses in a single quarter, so near-term estimates are more likely too low than too high.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"The 0.3-weight Defense Modernization exposure understates a budget-durable revenue stream that provides a growth floor.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Forward-deployed engineering headcount, not demand, is the binding constraint on deployment velocity, creating spend for integrator partners.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Regime probabilities are near-uniform (Goldilocks 26.3, Reflation 25.1, Contraction 24.9, Stagflation 23.7), so the macro label carries low conviction.","kind":"observed_fact"}],"confidence":0.55}},"technical":{"score":88,"passes":7,"criteria":{"above_150_200":true,"150_above_200":false,"200_rising_1m":true,"50_above_150_200":true,"above_50":true,"25pct_above_52w_low":true,"within_25pct_of_52w_high":true,"rs_positive_6m":true},"ready":true,"stage":"stage2_uptrend","close":191.79,"sma50":161.65,"sma150":146.54,"sma200":151.93,"sma150_prev4w":142.54,"sma150_declining":false,"pct_above_52w_low":78.8,"pct_from_52w_high":-7.4,"rs_6m":6.9,"rsi14":66.9,"atr20":7.174,"atr_pct":3.74,"overbought":false},"fundamentals":{"latest":{"period_end":"2026-06-30","filed":"2026-08-04","revenue":6155941000.0,"gross_profit":5220000000.0,"operating_income":2634652000.0,"net_income":3016692000.0,"ebitda":2663760000.0,"ocf":3400291000.0,"capex":42019000.0,"fcf":3358272000.0,"eps":1.17,"shares_diluted":2571169000.0,"cash":9409099000.0,"debt":0.0,"net_debt":-9409099000.0,"equity":9774194000.0,"total_assets":11678564000.0,"rnd":641239000.0,"sbc":835524000.0,"buybacks":null,"dividends":null,"gross_margin":0.8479613433592037,"operating_margin":0.4279852584682017,"net_margin":0.49004563234118065,"fcf_margin":0.5455334935796168,"fcf_conversion":1.1132299883448493,"revenue_growth":0.7892124221826102,"revenue_growth_prev":0.6770894863089338,"revenue_acceleration":0.11212293587367639,"eps_growth":2.9,"net_income_growth":2.9522122595284634,"fcf_growth":0.9653913141187707,"operating_margin_change":0.2624472267311754,"roic":2.1431739381656856,"incremental_roic":5.0,"operating_income_estimated":false,"financial":false,"roe":0.30863844118502254,"roa":0.25831018265601835,"net_debt_to_ebitda":-3.5322622908970778,"interest_coverage":null,"dilution":0.017861584080044235,"sbc_pct_revenue":0.1357264470208535,"tax_rate":0.05},"history":[{"period_end":"2022-09-30","filed":"2024-02-20","revenue":1830114000.0,"gross_profit":1438313000.0,"operating_income":-202318000.0,"net_income":-560771000.0,"ebitda":-182546000.0,"ocf":238401000.0,"capex":40953000.0,"fcf":197448000.0,"eps":-0.28,"sha